        "parts": "Entire version: no shape ablation at fixed parameters."
      },
      {
        "version": "V5",
        "parts": "Entire version: no loss scaling in other modalities or regimes."
      },
      {
        "version": "V7",
        "parts": "Entire version: no exponents or fitting choices compared."
      }
    ],
    "missing": [
      {
        "what": "Task-average OPT accuracy by size: visual 62.50→67.30→68.53→69.87; embodied 50.23→51.33→51.46→55.79.",
        "locator": "Table 2 and Table 3, Avg. column",
        "versions": "V6"
      },
      {
        "what": "Embodied average gain from scaling: +0.13 (1.3B→13B) and +4.46 (1.3B→175B). The authors use this as the 134x scaling reference.",
        "locator": "Table 5",
        "versions": "V6"
      }
    ],
    "verdict_notes": "Every row uses 50% chance as its baseline. For V6 the relevant comparison is across sizes within a task, so states were judged on each task's 4-point trend. Per-row states should be read per task group, not per size. Standard deviations are across prompts and often exceed the differences between sizes, e.g. Temperature 175B ±8.68. Only four model sizes are tested, so 'predictably' cannot be assessed beyond monotonicity. BERT and RoBERTa base/large and the YFCC-trained models are size comparisons too small to bear on scaling and are correctly omitted."
  },
